<DocsLayout
  title="Read implementation status before API shape."
  description="StateKnot is pre-alpha: bounded MCP Client/Server, static MCP Skills Server and Client/Host, and A2A 1.0 Client/Server profiles join the durable provider-native path; dynamic Skills, stable network Agent APIs, A2A gRPC, MCP Tasks, advanced graph semantics, and production qualification remain unfinished."
  section="Implementation status"
>
  <section aria-labelledby="status-matrix-title">
    <h2 id="status-matrix-title">Capability matrix</h2>
    <ul class="status-list">
      {
        capabilities.map((capability) => (
          <li class="status-item">
            <span class:list={["status-badge", capability.className]}>
              {capability.state}
            </span>
            <div>
              <h3>{capability.title}</h3>
              <p>{capability.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="claim-title">
    <h2 id="claim-title">What “implemented” means</h2>
    <p>
      Code and executable tests exist in the repository. Product crates are
      available as the exact <code>0.1.0-alpha.1</code> public preview, but that does
      not mean an API is stable, operational production gates pass, or production
      support has started. A v1 capability is supported only when implementation,
      tests, documentation, compatibility evidence, and release gates ship together.
      Read the <a href="/docs/versioning/">versioning and release policy</a> before
      depending on the preview.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="next-proof-title">
    <h2 id="next-proof-title">The next proof boundary</h2>
    <p>
      The 32-case Runtime matrix now proves real overlap with canonical sibling
      commits, higher-fence orphan takeover, ordered read-only Tool waves, and
      serialized write barriers on PostgreSQL 16 and 17. The strict MCP binding
      retains end-to-end PostgreSQL recovery evidence. The separate general Tool
      client and OAuth provider now pass all 32 frozen scored client scenarios,
      including all 25 OAuth scenarios: 371 scored assertions succeed and none
      fail. The Server profile passes all 37 scored Server scenarios with 114
      successes, five skips, one Info, and zero failures or warnings. The A2A
      1.0 Server gate adds 177 official TCK passes, 88 declared skips, and zero
      failures/errors/xfails. The durable A2A Client now adds an
      eleven-operation, dual-binding loopback matrix and real PostgreSQL
      durable-before-dispatch/Unknown/no-redispatch evidence, plus bounded
      operator-attested context/history and message-ID recovery. Durable
      terminal-task recovery now polls both bindings directly without a business
      resend; migration 17→18, immutable registry, conditional object
      publication, multipart ingestion, authorization-first reads, and full
      digest verification all have executable PostgreSQL and object-store
      evidence. Official Client/live-peer and recovery-attestation
      qualification, dynamic MCP Skills, Skill-byte materialization, MCP Tasks,
      and other client extensions remain separate gates.
    </p>
  </section>

